    "turn_text": "Like a very high stakes game of chicken, the Senate on Monday rejected two bills. First, the Republicans on mass voted against a continuing resolution that would fund the government until December and extend the debt ceiling until December of 2022. The vote was 48 to 50. More on that in a moment. Then the Democrats voted down a Republican effort to fund the government until December, but without the increase in the debt limit. Following that stalemate, Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer spoke from the floor.",
